  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved governance of labour migration and mobility in line with ILS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ILO is working with tripartite constituents in Lebanon to enhance the governance of labour migration, improve the protection of migrant workers, ensuring their decent work along with a fair sharing of the prosperity they help to create and to strengthen the capacity of ILO constituents in designing and implementing measures to promote decent work in the care economy. This is in line with the ILO Strategy on Labour Migration 2024-2027, informed by the ILO Centenary Declaration for the Future of Work, the ILO Fair Migration Agenda, the 2017 ILC Conclusions concerning fair and effective labour migration governance, the Singapore Statement, adopted at the 17th Asia and the Pacific Regional Meeting (APRM) in December 2022,  the Bali Declaration, adopted at the ILO 16th APRM in December 2016, and the ILO Resolution on Decent Work and the Care Economy (2024). To achieve this, ILO efforts will focus on establishing or strengthening institutional mechanisms to implement and monitor governance frameworks on labour migration taking account also of the political and economic situation in Lebanon. Efforts will also be made to contribute to advancing policy and legislation for better protection of migrant workers and refugees in line with relevant ILS (including the FPRW, Conventions Nos. 97, 143, 181, 189, 190 and their related Recommendations), the ILO Multilateral Framework for Labour Migration (2006), the ILO Guiding Principles on the access of refugees and other forcibly displaced persons to the labour market (2016), and the ILO General Principles and Operational Guidelines for Fair Recruitment and the Definition of Recruitment Fees and Related Costs (2019). ILO will work to strengthen the capacities of ILO constituents in promoting decent work in the care economy. During this biennium, ILO will offer its services through evidence- based policy advice and research; capacity building and training; engagement of social partners; and monitoring of impact and promotion of good p</narrative>
  </description>
